"The Cox model predicts a recurrence-free survival time of 330 months, with no recurrence event observed during the follow-up period. This prediction is based on the patient's age of 72 and a PSA level of 6.9, which are known prognostic factors for prostate cancer recurrence risk. The T1c staging derived from the digital rectal examination provides baseline information regarding the extent of the disease, though long-term recurrence risk remains subject to clinical follow-up."